  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "slug": "cluster",
      "term": "Cluster",
      "definition": "Three trebles worked into the same chain-space, joined at the top. The basic building block of the granny square."
    },
    {
      "slug": "chain-space",
      "term": "Chain space",
      "definition": "The gap created by skipping a chain or chains. Corner chain-2 spaces hold the corner cluster pairs; side chain-1 spaces separate cluster pairs along the sides."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": ["crochet-magic-ring", "crochet-working-in-the-round"],
  "criticalTechniques": ["crochet-magic-ring"],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The eight-round granny square builds to a 20 cm motif in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook — large enough to use as a standalone pot holder, a small cushion-cover front, or the centrepiece panel in a granny-stitch blanket with a plain border surround. The construction follows the same rule as every granny square: each round adds one more "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "cluster" } }],
            "text": "cluster"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " group per side, so round 8 carries seven side clusters on each of the four edges."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "At 20 cm, the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "chain-space" } }],
            "text": "chain-space"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " structure at the corners becomes an important reference point while you work. Placing a stitch marker in each corner ch-2 space at the start of round 4 or 5 helps keep track of corners on the longer rounds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Materials for one motif",
          "body": "About 20 g of DK-weight cotton in one to eight colours. A 4 mm crochet hook (UK 8, US G/6). Tapestry needle. Scissors. A blocking mat and pins are recommended — an 8-round square benefits from thorough pinning."
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Gauge" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each finished eight-round granny square measures 20 × 20 cm in DK-weight cotton with a 4 mm hook, after steam-blocking. Make a six-round test motif first and check it measures 15 cm — that confirms your tension is right before committing to the full eight rounds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Stitches used" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "chain (ch) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "slip stitch (sl st) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "treble (tr) — UK; called double crochet (dc) in US patterns." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "magic ring (MR) — adjustable starting loop; no centre hole." }] }] }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Pattern" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked in the round, right side facing throughout. Ch 3 at the start of each round counts as the first treble of the first cluster. Do not turn. Place a stitch marker in the starting ch-3 of each round to make the join easier to find."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 1" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Form a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 2 tr into the ring. *Ch 2, 3 tr into the ring*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 2, sl st to top of beg ch-3. Pull tail to close ring. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 2" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st across next 2 tr and into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. *Ch 1, into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr)*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 1, sl st to top of beg ch-3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 4 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Rounds 3 to 7" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each round follows the same pattern: sl st into first ch-2 corner sp; ch 3; into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr; ch 1; *work 3 tr into each ch-1 side sp with ch 1 between each group until the next corner; into corner ch-2 sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr); ch 1*; repeat for all four sides; sl st to beg ch-3. Stitch counts per round: Round 3 (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 8 ch-1 sides). Round 4 (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 12 ch-1 sides). Round 5 (60 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 16 ch-1 sides). Round 6 (72 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 20 ch-1 sides). Round 7 (84 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 24 ch-1 sides.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 8" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *[Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] six times. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. [Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] six times. Sl st to top of beg ch-3. (96 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 28 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Chart" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The chart reads outward from the magic ring. The corner ch-2 spaces are the fixed landmarks; count side cluster groups per edge to check you are on the right round."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "definition": {
            "title": "Granny square — eight rounds",
            "layout": "round",
